{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEMkQ7yDkPhhueLZya4a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found two problems in `api.py` and fixed both. The 5 existing tests still pass. I didn't write new tests for the fixes, and I didn't start the server to try them.\n\n- **Private tasks could be liked or view-counted by anyone.** `POST /tasks/{id}/like` and `/view` had no access check. For example, bob could change the counters on alice's private task #1, and a 200 response confirmed the task existed. Both now return 403 unless the caller owns the task or it's public, as the README says.\n- **`PATCH /tasks/{id}` accepted bad values.** `title` could be empty or not a string, and `visibility` could be anything. Only the owner can edit, so this isn't a cross-user hole, but it could corrupt a task. It now validates the same way `POST /tasks` does.\n\nI checked the other endpoints and they were already correct. Reading a task, commenting and nudging respect visibility. Editing, deleting and completing are owner-only. A missing or unknown token gets 401, and `GET /tasks` lists only your own tasks plus public ones.\n\nI left a few things alone and listed them in `ANSWER.md`:\n- **Dev tokens:** they're hardcoded and published in the README, so replace them before launch.\n- **404 vs 403:** a missing task returns 404 and a private one returns 403, so private task ids can be told apart from missing ones. The README specifies 403, so I kept it.\n- **Rate limiting:** there is none, so likes, views and nudges on public tasks can be inflated.\n\nI didn't commit anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1105,"cache_read_input_tokens":23711,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1105},"output_tokens":508,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_